{"availability":"available","full":"Sahilll15/interview-coach","name":"interview-coach","description":"Spoken mock interviews in the browser over the OpenAI Realtime API, with a report that scores each answer using quotes from your own words.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-02T22:35:12Z","updated":"2026-10-03T20:26:10Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://interview-coach-seven-rose.vercel.app","topics":["ai","nextjs","openai","realtime-api","typescript","vercel"],"demo":"https://interview-coach-seven-rose.vercel.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T15:46:30.703Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T15:46:30.703Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T15:46:30.703Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T15:46:30.703Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A spoken mock interview in the browser that scores each answer and quotes your own words back to you.","Most people prepare for interviews by rehearsing answers in their head, which hides the rambling and the missing results. Interview Coach lets you paste a job description (or pick a sample role), choose a level and an interview type, and talk to an AI interviewer for about four and a half minutes. You then get a report that scores every answer, quotes what you said, and gives you three practice questions aimed at your gaps. No mic? Text mode runs the same interviewer and the same report."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Sahilll15/interview-coach/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"1ebea10aeec57e1871077a187b3d94438a997794544bb7bc65d9e072191b5fb5","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T15:46:30.815Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T15:46:30.815Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A spoken mock interview in the browser that scores each answer and quotes your own words back to you.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Sahilll15/interview-coach/blob/main/README.md"},"aud